## Goal
Clarify in ADR 0007 (failure notification after a failed "Remember") how a pending notification behaves when the user quits explicitly (DEV-50).

## Problems
None.

## Decision
`docs/adr/0007-remember-failure-notification.md` now separates two cases:
- The idle quit does not end the app while the permission prompt or delivery is pending. The waits stay capped at 60 s for the prompt and 5 s for delivery.
- An explicit quit (logout, Quit) keeps the 10 s cap from ADR 0005. A logout must not wait a minute for a banner, so a notification still pending at that point is dropped.

Dropping it costs nothing: the link is already open and the log line is already written (decision 5 of the ADR). The wording of the idle-quit sentence was also tightened to "idle quit" so it no longer reads as covering explicit quits.

